@api = http://localhost:5000

### Health (anonymous): overall status plus database and kafka checks
GET {{api}}/health

### Log in as a seeded officer (every demo user's password is Passw0rd!)
# Other users: claimant1@ / claimant2@ / officer1..4@ / manager@claimdesk.test
# @name login
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "officer1@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Who am I? Uses the token from the login request above
GET {{api}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token: 401 ProblemDetails
GET {{api}}/api/auth/me

### Wrong password: 401 ProblemDetails (same answer as an unknown email)
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-wrong-password

{
  "email": "officer1@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "wrong"
}

# ======================================================================
# Claimant slice. Run top to bottom. Dates use the VS Code REST Client
# {{$localDatetime}} helper; in other clients type a recent yyyy-MM-dd date.
# ======================================================================

### Log in as claimant1 (holds POL-SG-0001 Motor, POL-SG-0002 Property, POL-MY-*, POL-ID-0001)
# @name claimant1
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "claimant1@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Submit a motor claim on POL-SG-0001: 201 + Location, status Submitted, event staged in the outbox
# @name submitted
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-submit-1

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-SG-0001",
  "productType": "Motor",
  "incidentDate": "{{$localDatetime 'YYYY-MM-DD' -1 d}}",
  "description": "Rear-ended at a junction; bumper and tail lamp damaged.",
  "claimedAmount": 1250.50,
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### My claims, newest first
# @name mine
GET {{api}}/api/claims/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}

### One claim with timeline and open information requests
GET {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Product the policy does not cover: 409 ProblemDetails
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-SG-0001",
  "productType": "Property",
  "incidentDate": "{{$localDatetime 'YYYY-MM-DD' -1 d}}",
  "description": "Kitchen flooded.",
  "claimedAmount": 800.00,
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### Missing fields: 400 validation ProblemDetails
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-SG-0001"
}

### Log in as claimant2
# @name claimant2
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "claimant2@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### claimant2 reading claimant1's claim: 403 ProblemDetails
GET {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant2.response.body.accessToken}}

### claimant2 claiming on claimant1's policy: 404 (indistinguishable from an unknown policy)
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant2.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-SG-0001",
  "productType": "Motor",
  "incidentDate": "{{$localDatetime 'YYYY-MM-DD' -1 d}}",
  "description": "Not my policy.",
  "claimedAmount": 100.00,
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### Unknown claim: 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{api}}/api/claims/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Answering an information request.
# claimant1 has one seeded claim in AwaitingInformation (POL-MY-0001, windscreen).
# Paste its id from the "My claims" response above (the entry with "status": "AwaitingInformation").
@awaitingClaimId = paste-claim-id-here

# @name awaiting
GET {{api}}/api/claims/{{awaitingClaimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Answer the open request: 200, status back to UnderReview, InformationProvided in the outbox.
# Sending it a second time gives 409 (the claim is no longer awaiting information).
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{awaitingClaimId}}/information-requests/{{awaiting.response.body.openInformationRequests[0].id}}/response
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Police report reference PR-2026-0415."
}

# ======================================================================
# Officer slice. Run the claimant section first: it uses {{submitted}}
# (claimant1's new SG motor claim) and the claimant1 token.
# Commands need the officer assigned to the claim; anyone else gets 403.
# ======================================================================

### Log in as officer1
# @name officer1
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "officer1@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Log in as officer2
# @name officer2
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "officer2@claimdesk.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Unassigned queue (default scope), most urgent SLA first; seeded claims are slaBreached: true
GET {{api}}/api/claims/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Unassigned Singapore claims, first page of 5
GET {{api}}/api/claims/queue?scope=unassigned&market=Singapore&page=1&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}

### officer1 picks up the submitted claim: 200, UnderReview
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-assign-1

### officer2 tries to pick up the same claim: 409 (already taken)
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{officer2.response.body.accessToken}}

### officer1's own queue (UnderReview, AwaitingInformation, Approved), filtered by status
GET {{api}}/api/claims/queue?scope=mine&status=UnderReview
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}

### officer2 working officer1's claim: 403
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/information-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{officer2.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Not my claim."
}

### Ask the claimant for information: 200, AwaitingInformation, request in openInformationRequests
# @name infoRequested
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/information-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Please upload photos of the damage and the workshop quotation."
}

### claimant1 answers: back to UnderReview
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/information-requests/{{infoRequested.response.body.openInformationRequests[0].id}}/response
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Photos and quotation uploaded."
}

### Decision before a reserve is recorded: 409
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "Rejected",
  "reason": "Too early."
}

### Record the reserve and notes (status unchanged)
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/assessment
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserveAmount": 1200.00,
  "currency": "SGD",
  "notes": "Workshop quotation checked against photos."
}

### Approve without an amount: 400 validation ProblemDetails
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "Approved",
  "reason": "Covered loss."
}

### Approve: 200, Approved (amount must be in the claim currency and within the maximum payable)
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "Approved",
  "approvedAmount": 1200.00,
  "currency": "SGD",
  "reason": "Covered loss; amount agreed with the workshop."
}

### Settle: 200, Settled. Sending it again gives 409.
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted.response.body.id}}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Reject example: claimant1 submits a second claim
# @name submitted2
POST {{api}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimant1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-SG-0002",
  "productType": "Property",
  "incidentDate": "{{$localDatetime 'YYYY-MM-DD' -1 d}}",
  "description": "Ceiling stain from a slow leak over several months.",
  "claimedAmount": 900.00,
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### officer1 assigns it
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted2.response.body.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}

### ...records a reserve
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted2.response.body.id}}/assessment
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reserveAmount": 900.00,
  "currency": "SGD"
}

### ...and rejects it: 200, Rejected (a rejection takes no amount)
POST {{api}}/api/claims/{{submitted2.response.body.id}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "Rejected",
  "reason": "Gradual leaks are excluded by the policy wording."
}
